<!--
The chrome every blog post wears, nested INSIDE the site `Layout`: declared on
`<Route path="blog">` in `main.bsx`, it reaches every post and nothing else, and
adds only what an article has (no document, no header or footer).

<ArticleHeader/> renders the title, byline and date from the post's frontmatter,
and nothing for the undated blog index. The comments are the replies to the
post's announcement on Bluesky, read live in a server island so the page itself
stays cacheable; its fallback, shown until the island swaps in, is the link to
reply. A post with no announcement renders neither.
-->
<ArticleHeader/>
<Slot/>
<ServerIsland name="comments" {CacheHeaders{edge_max_age: "60s"}}>
	<StandardSiteComments/>
	<StandardSiteReplyLink slot="fallback"/>
</ServerIsland>
